 "defaultCounty": "los-angeles-county",
 "singular": [
  "California charges a vehicle license fee of 0.65% of the purchase price instead of a property tax, and it shrinks for 11 renewal years on a fixed schedule (100%, 90%, 80%... down to 15%) [dmv-vlf].",
  "The VLF restarts at 100% when a car changes hands: a used car bought for $18,000 pays VLF on $18,000, not on its original sticker price [dmv-vlf].",
  "The Transportation Improvement Fee adds $33 to $231 a year depending on the vehicle's value, in five brackets [dmv-fees].",
  "Zero-emission vehicles of model year 2020 and later pay a $121 Road Improvement Fee at each renewal, but not at the first registration of a new ZEV bought from a dealer [dmv-fees].",
  "A trade-in does not reduce California sales tax: on a $20,000 car with a $4,000 trade-in, tax is due on $20,000 [cdtfa-dealers].",
  "Use tax follows the buyer's home address, from 7.25% in many rural counties to 11% in Long Beach (rates effective October 1, 2026) [cdtfa-rates].",
  "Gasoline and hybrid cars skip the smog check for their first eight model years and pay a smog abatement fee at renewal instead; electric cars never need one [bar-faq].",
  "Smog check prices are set by each station, not by the state; only the $8.25 certificate fee is fixed [bar-faq].",
  "Dealer document fees are capped at $85 for dealers that register cars electronically with the DMV, and $70 for the others [doc-fee]."
 ],
 "sources": {
